# Koradiya Group IMPEX — Public Website (Frontend Repo)

This repo contains **one file**, `index.html` — the public Koradiya Group IMPEX
site. It's a static page: no server, no build step. In the browser it reads
its text, images, products and every **E-Catalogue** entry directly from
Supabase (the same database the private admin repo writes to).

This repo is meant to be **public**. It's safe to be public — the only key
embedded in it is the Supabase **anon public** key, which is designed to be
exposed in browsers; your actual data stays protected by Row Level Security
rules defined in the backend repo's `schema.sql`, not by hiding this key.

## 1. Connect it to your Supabase project

1. Open `index.html` in a text editor.
2. Near the top of `<head>`, find:
   ```html
   window.SUPABASE_CONFIG = {
     url: "",
     anonKey: ""
   };
   ```
3. Fill in your Supabase **Project URL** and **anon public** key
   (Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API). These come from the same
   Supabase project the backend repo's `schema.sql` was run in.
4. Commit and push.

If you leave `SUPABASE_CONFIG` blank, the page still works — it just shows
its built-in fallback content instead of live data from the database.

## 2. Deploy

Any static host works. Two easy options:

### Option A — Render Static Site (free)
1. [render.com](https://render.com) → **New → Static Site** → connect this repo.
2. **Build Command:** leave blank. **Publish Directory:** `.`
3. Deploy. Render gives you a URL like `https://koradiya-group-impex.onrender.com`.
4. Every push to your connected branch redeploys automatically.

### Option B — Netlify / Vercel / Cloudflare Pages / GitHub Pages
All of these work the same way for a single static HTML file: connect the
repo, no build command, publish directory `.` (or `/`).

## What updates automatically vs. what needs a redeploy

- **Automatic, no redeploy** — anything edited in the admin backend (page
  text, images, products, **E-Catalogue** names/categories/PDFs, contact
  email): these all live in Supabase and the page fetches them fresh on
  every load.
- **Needs a redeploy** — only the one-time `SUPABASE_CONFIG` connection
  above, or any structural change to `index.html` itself.

## Where everything else lives

- The **backoffice/admin app** (`admin.html`) and the **database schema**
  (`schema.sql`) live in the separate **private** backend repo — they're
  not in this repo on purpose, since the admin app is how someone edits
  the live site and shouldn't be public.
- The **database** itself is Supabase — not hosted in either repo.
